% =============================================================================
% CHAPTER 1: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
% =============================================================================
\chapter{Executive Summary}
\cleardoublepage

\section{Overview}
WAuth (Warehouse Auth) is a Python library designed for secure, machine-locked encrypted secret management. The system provides a robust mechanism for storing, rotating, backing up, and retrieving secrets that are encrypted using Fernet (AES-128-CBC) and tied to the specific machine where they were created.

The library addresses a critical security requirement in modern software development: the need to store sensitive information such as API keys, database credentials, and certificates in a secure manner that prevents accidental leakage across different environments.

\section{Key Findings}

\subsection{System Strengths}
\begin{enumerate}
	\item \textbf{Strong Encryption Architecture}: Fernet (AES-128-CBC) provides authenticated encryption with AES-128 in CBC mode with PKCS7 padding, combined with HMAC-SHA256 for message authentication.
	\item \textbf{Machine-Locking Mechanism}: Keys are derived from machine-specific identifiers, preventing cross-machine decryption.
	\item \textbf{Dual Driver Architecture}: Factory pattern supports both local encrypted vaults and Docker secrets seamlessly.
	\item \textbf{TTL Support}: Automatic secret expiration reduces attack surface.
	\item \textbf{Comprehensive Exception Hierarchy}: Structured error handling enables precise error management.
	\item \textbf{High Code Quality}: Pylint score of 9.95/10 and 98\% test coverage demonstrate production-grade quality.
\end{enumerate}

\subsection{Technical Audit Results}
\begin{table}[htbp]
	\centering
	\caption{Code Quality Metrics}
	\label{tbl:quality-metrics}
	\begin{tabular}{|l|c|c|}
