\chapter{Scalability \& Stress Projections}
\cleardoublepage

\section{Theoretical Load Analysis}
WAuth is designed for single-machine secret storage. This section analyzes behavior under increased load scenarios.

\subsection{Single Instance Projections}
\begin{table}[htbp]
	\centering
	\caption{Scalability Projections - Single Machine}
	\label{tbl:scalability-single}
	\begin{tabular}{|l|c|c|c|p{5cm}|}
		\hline
		\textbf{Metric}    & \textbf{1x} & \textbf{10x} & \textbf{100x} & \textbf{Assessment}                                             \\
		\hline
		Secrets Stored     & 1,000       & 10,000       & 100,000       & SQLite handles efficiently up to 100K records                   \\
		\hline
		Concurrent Access  & 10          & 100          & 1,000         & File locking prevents corruption; performance degrades linearly \\
		\hline
		Key Operations/sec & 1,000       & 500          & 100           & Encryption overhead becomes significant at scale                \\
		\hline
		Memory Usage       & 50MB        & 200MB        & 2GB           & Scales with secret count due to Python object overhead          \\
		\hline
		Database Size      & 1MB         & 10MB         & 100MB         & Compressed storage; Fernet tokens add ~40\% overhead            \\
		\hline
	\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\subsection{Bottleneck Analysis}
\begin{enumerate}
	\item \textbf{CPU-Bound Encryption}: Fernet encryption is computationally intensive; expect 50-100ms per 10K operations under 10x load
	\item \textbf{SQLite Concurrency}: Single-writer limitation creates bottlenecks at high concurrent access
	\item \textbf{Memory Footprint}: Python objects for each secret maintain references in memory
\end{enumerate}

\section{Stress Testing Recommendations}
\begin{enumerate}
	\item \textbf{Base Load (1x)}: 1,000 secrets, 10 concurrent requests - Expected: <10ms latency
	\item \textbf{Moderate Load (10x)}: 10,000 secrets, 100 concurrent requests - Expected: 10-50ms latency
	\item \textbf{High Load (100x)}: 100,000 secrets, 1,000 concurrent requests - Expected: 50-500ms latency
	\item \textbf{Saturation Point}: >100 concurrent write operations causes significant degradation
\end{enumerate}

\section{Horizontal Scaling Strategy}
For enterprise deployments requiring horizontal scaling:

\begin{enumerate}
	\item \textbf{Key Distribution}: Use custom keys with external key management
	\item \textbf{Read Replicas}: Implement read-heavy workloads with replicas
	\item \textbf{Connection Pooling}: Use persistent connections to reduce overhead
	\item \textbf{Caching Layer}: Implement Redis for frequently accessed secrets
	\item \textbf{Secret Rotation}: Regular rotation prevents accumulation
\end{enumerate}

\cleardoublepage

